From 0bb0213534db663401096402eeb5caa96eed19fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Bruel <christian.bruel@foss.st.com>
Date: Thu, 7 May 2026 14:25:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: st: Free iATU window used by I/O BAR on
 stm32mp25.

The MP25 has four iATU windows: three are used for I/O and memory BARs,
and one is used for CFG accesses. With the addition of PME_Turn_Off
support, enabled via the 'use_atu_msg' attribute, an extra window is
required to map the MSG TLP region.

Since I/O BARs are legacy and rarely used, drop their support and reuse
the freed iATU entry for the PME message TLP.

Signed-off-by: Christian Bruel <christian.bruel@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I52d2fbb33108d293520316d7674d1dcbb2b7cfe1
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/565057
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Fabrice GASNIER <fabrice.gasnier@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Fabrice GASNIER <fabrice.gasnier@foss.st.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/st/stm32mp251.dtsi | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/st/stm32mp251.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/st/stm32mp251.dtsi
index 122e7f647004..cc5b1c9a9bb9 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/st/stm32mp251.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/st/stm32mp251.dtsi
@@ -2319,8 +2319,7 @@ pcie_rc: pcie@48400000 {
 						<0 0 0 4 &intc 0 0 GIC_SPI 267 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 				#address-cells = <3>;
 				#size-cells = <2>;
-				ranges = <0x01000000 0x0 0x00000000 0x10010000 0x0 0x10000>,
-					 <0x02000000 0x0 0x10020000 0x10020000 0x0 0x7fe0000>,
+				ranges = <0x02000000 0x0 0x10010000 0x10010000 0x0 0x7ff0000>,
 					 <0x42000000 0x0 0x18000000 0x18000000 0x0 0x8000000>;
 				dma-ranges = <0x42000000 0x0 0x80000000 0x80000000 0x0 0x80000000>;
 				clocks = <&scmi_clk CK_SCMI_ICN_PCIE>;
-- 
